# Deny list for scripts/check-pii.mjs. Copy to `.pii-names`, which is gitignored.
#
#   cp .pii-names.example .pii-names
#
# One name per line. `#` starts a comment. Matching is case-sensitive and on word
# boundaries, so a capitalised name in prose is caught while a lowercase identifier that
# happens to contain it is not.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NOT THE LIST. The obvious shortcut is to keep the names inline in
# check-pii.mjs, reasoning that anyone who can read the list can already read the
# repository. That is true of the access and false of the goal: the point is that these
# names are not in a commit at all, and a checker that carries them republishes every one
# of them, permanently, in the file doing the purging. The sister repo made exactly that
# mistake and had to rewrite history to undo it.
#
# So the names live on the machines that push, and never in a commit. If you clone this
# repository the check still runs its identifier patterns and tells you, loudly, that it
# has no name list.
#
# Put first names in as well as full ones. Next to a repository about somebody's personal
# notes -- and Vault Shelf shelves notes BY PERSON, so a person is a first-class object
# here in a way it was not next door -- a first name plus a note count is identifying.

# Colleagues, family, anyone who appears in the vault:
# Firstname
# Firstname Lastname

# TYPED ENTRIES (github#106). The rules that would name you -- your employer, your work
# tracker, your vault -- live here for the same reason the names do. A line `kind: value`
# adds a rule instead of a name; any kind other than these three is refused:
#
#   email: example.com     # someone@example.com is a hit
#   jira: ABC              # ABC-123 is a hit (case-sensitive, word boundaries)
#   vault: MyVault         # C:\MyVault or D:/MyVault is a hit
#
# Repeat a kind for more values. A list that declares no entry of some kind warns here and
# FAILS in CI. CI reads the PII_NAMES repository secret instead of this file: the same
# entries, comma-separated on one line, e.g.
#
#   Firstname,Firstname Lastname,email: example.com,jira: ABC,vault: MyVault
#
# Every loaded value is also planted into a synthetic line on every run, and has to be
# caught by its own rule. A control that fails prints its kind and index, never the value.
